        <item>
            <title>0.12.0</title>
            <pubDate>Sun, 16 Aug 2026 20:16:34 +0700</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>0.12.0</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.12.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>What's new in 0.12.0</h2>
<ul>
<li>The pill library learned your habits: the Suggestions tile (formerly &quot;Clipboard&quot;) now also lists the shortcuts you actually press in the app that was in front when you opened the menu — newest first, named from the app&#x27;s own menu bar with the keys beneath. Drag one onto a ring and it becomes a Switch + Shortcut pill for that app. Reflexes like ⌘C/⌘V, your own triggers and shortcuts already on a ring are left out</li>
<li>The Tray: collect pills while arranging and drop the copies into another menu. Opening the library always lands on the categories; pull down for the A-Z list, and the pill you drag rides above the library on its way out</li>
<li>Escape now backs out exactly one step: an open confirm, then a folder, then a sub-menu, then the menu — and inside an editor window it closes that window. Closing an editor with unsaved edits asks Save / Discard / Cancel; Cancel on an edit page really discards, the ring snaps back</li>
<li>The ✓/✕ confirm beside a pill inside a folder emerges from under its pill and retracts into it at the folder&#x27;s own pace; it always sits above its neighbours, and backing out of it sounds like navigation, not a refusal</li>
<li>Editor windows open beside the ring — right of it, left if there&#x27;s no room — and every page of the editor re-places itself there; the pointer no longer jumps when an editor opens or after cancelling a confirm</li>
<li>The little name/shortcut bubble on hover now sits on the line from the centre through the pill, for every pill</li>
<li>The &quot;3D light&quot; rim around the hub and pills is gone for good</li>
<li>Compass: the hub no longer leans toward the pointer; ↑/↓ select a pill, ←/→ switch between the universal menus; holding a navigation key no longer machine-guns; the menu closes with the same sound it opened with, and cancelling keeps its own sound</li>
<li>The pointer trail shows only while you&#x27;re using the menu — never in arrange mode or under an editor</li>
<li>Right-clicking the hub: the gear now gives the same feedback as the pencil on a pill</li>
<li>Folder feel: a folder you close by pulling back stays closed until you step off the pill and come back; the goo strand no longer sticks out after a folder closes, and it stops short of coloured pills</li>
<li>Safeguards in the editor sit 2×2 with the undo seconds on their own row; the undo cancel target aims where the pill actually flew, inside folders too</li>
<li>Smoother openings: the menu is fully drawn before it appears (no half-drawn frames after long idles or on the first open after wake), and swapping between menus keeps the pills together with their bodies</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
